# Dependencies for the SDK phase gates ONLY. The dual-target conformance harness
# (dual_target.py) is deliberately stdlib-only and needs nothing from this file.
#
# P0's gate is "official Python SDK auth.me() against localhost returns Identity" and P1's is a
# Python+Node SDK smoke across scopes. Both are acceptance tests whose whole point is that the
# UNMODIFIED official client works against our base URL, so the version is pinned exactly: an
# unpinned gate that passes against a newer client than the plan surveyed is not the gate the plan
# specifies. 0.5.9 is the version whose source was read during P-1 and from which
# reference/types_dump.txt and reference/endpoints.txt were extracted.
#
# Install into a throwaway venv at gate time, not into the system environment:
#   python3 -m venv .venv-gate && .venv-gate/bin/pip install -r conformance/requirements-gate.txt
# .venv-gate is gitignored.
#
# Bumping this version is an upstream-drift decision, not maintenance: diff the new spec, decide
# adopt/pin per change, record it in the plan. See the plan's "Upstream drift" section.
agentmail==0.5.9
